    "durationMs": 232636,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n- **Laravel 11 / PHP 8.3** scaffolded into `/workspace` via Composer (created in a subdir, moved in around the existing `.git`), with dependencies installed.\n- **Endpoints** registered via `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''` so paths are exactly `/links`, `/links/{code}`, `/r/{code}` — no `/api` prefix.\n- **`LinkController`** handles everything with manual JSON parsing/validation so every error path returns `{\"error\": ...}` with the right status: 201 create (generated 8-char codes, custom codes 4-20 chars `[A-Za-z0-9_-]`), 409 duplicate custom code (unique index backstop for races), 404 unknown codes, 422 for malformed JSON/missing/invalid url/invalid code. URLs are returned byte-identical (unescaped slashes in JSON). `/r/{code}` does an atomic `clicks + 1` then 302s to the stored URL.\n- **Persistence**: `links` table in MySQL read entirely from the `DB_*` env vars — `.env` contains no DB settings, so nothing is hard-coded.\n- **`start.sh`** (executable): runs `php artisan migrate --force`, then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground, as required.\n- **README** has a \"Starting the server\" section.\n\nTesting: a 34-check curl suite passed clean — including duplicate/conflict handling, boundary code lengths (4 and 20), unicode/query URLs returned unchanged, click increments of exactly one per redirect, and list ordering/total. I also killed and restarted the server to confirm click counts survive restarts (2 → redirect → 3), verified migrations no-op on second start, and left port 8000 free for the harness to run `sh start.sh` itself."
  }
